From 91c3ea485acff1b36645ab9cc35fda04d06cf22a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tryinget <markus@team-wangler.de>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:04:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] feat(frame): frame.diagnose compares DOM, extension and
 CDP frame views

Widgets that live in srcdoc or script-created iframes show up as
about:blank frames, sandboxed frames never load the content script,
and out-of-process frames are visible to CDP only. Each inventory
alone hides a different half of the picture, and the usual symptom is
a selector that never matches.

frame.diagnose collects three inventories side by side and explains
the mismatches:

- DOM <iframe> elements with src/srcdoc, sandbox, allow and layout
  (collected through a CDP evaluate),
- chrome.webNavigation frames (the ids frame.switch uses) with a
  content-script PING per frame,
- the CDP frame tree (the ids frame.js uses).

src/utils/frame-diagnose.ts holds the pure correlation and the warning
rules: blank/srcdoc frames, sandboxes without allow-scripts, zero-size
frames, unreachable content scripts, navigation errors, CDP-only
frames, cross-origin frames, ambiguous URL matches and count
mismatches. Each warning names the frame command that still works.

Registered as a tab-lane tool in tool-scope, the MCP server and the CLI
(plain-text report; --json for the full inventories).

